---
# ansible-lint scans everything beneath the path it is given, and `make deps`
# installs third-party collections into ansible/.collections -- gitignored,
# vendored code this repo does not own or ship.
#
# Without this, `make lint` on any machine that has run `make deps` reports
# errors from community.general's own sanity-ignore files: nobody here can fix
# them, they change with every collection release, and they bury the findings
# that do matter. A linter whose output is mostly noise stops being read.
#
# CI never saw this. Its lint job installs ansible with pip and never runs
# `make deps`, so ansible/.collections does not exist there -- which is
# precisely why it only surfaced once the linters were installed on a real
# workstation.
#
# .yamllint already ignores the same directory for the same reason; this
# brings ansible-lint into line with it rather than introducing a new policy.
exclude_paths:
  - ansible/.collections/
